ns.\n\n**`move`:**\n- The rule `need amount = 0 or from != to else SameAccount` is now `need from != to else SameAccount`.\n- The example `move A A 0` used to expect `ok` and now expects `SameAccount`.\n- Its other guarantees and its body are unchanged.\n\n**`tip`** also needed a change. It calls `move` directly, and `tip A A 0` is supposed to succeed and emit `Tipped`. Under the new rule that call would have been refused. So `tip` now only calls `move` when the amount is greater than 0. A move of 0 changed nothing anyway, so `tip` behaves exactly as before. I added the example `tip A A 0 -> ok` to pin that down.\n\n**Other callers:** `capture`, `refund` and `split` already refuse the same-account case before they call `move`, and `purchase` only reaches `move` through `capture`. None of them needed changes, and all re-proved clean.", "ttft_ms": 2089, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 32765, "uuid": "c3ba4905-9583-4e6c-87c7-4e015ba7ea5d", "ttft_stream_ms": 1317, "time_to_request_ms": 25, "first_content_frame_ms": 1317, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0, "model_usage_since_last_result": {"claude-opus-5-5": {"inputTokens": 12, "outputTokens": 2753, "cacheReadInputTokens": 59675, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 13693, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.176587, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 287, "cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens": 13693, "canonicalModel": "claude-opus-5-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "credential_expires_at": "2026-11-04T19:57:08.746Z"}